    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="letterhead">YALE UNIVERSITY CHRISTIAN ASSOCIATION
                        <lb/>DWIGHT HALL <lb/><!--auf der rechten Blattseite--><rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__770" type="place">NEW HAVEN</rs>, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__726" type="place"
                        >CONNECTICUT</rs></fw><dateline>404A Yale Station <lb/>Wednesday, <date
                            when="1946-04-10">April 10</date>.</dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Mr.
                        Tillich</rs>,</salute></opener>
                <p>I imagine you must have been wondering about my silence after <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3471" type="person">Franziska</rs> had told you
                    that we wanted very much to have you come to Yale for a
                    discussi<!-- evtl. abgeschnitten --> group. The delay has been in choosing the
                    boys to participate – which had to be done carefully, as we wanted to keep the
                    group small enough for convenient and effective discussion – and in<pb n="2"/>
                    setting a proliminary meeting. The upshot is that a group of nine boys will meet
                    next Tuesday, <date when="1946-04-16">April 16</date>, to discuss your chapter
                    in <hi rend="u"><rs ref="#tillich__ZATSNTWD" type="work">The Christian
                            Answer</rs></hi>.<note type="ea">Gemeint ist der Artikel: <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Tillich, Paul</rs>: <q><rs
                                ref="#tillich__MPIUNK3W" type="work">The World Situation</rs></q>.
                        Auch enthalten in: <rs ref="#tillich__DZNKRWUT" type="work">Main
                            Works/Hauptwerke II</rs>, 165–194.</note> We feel that we can profit
                    more from a meeting with you if we have this opportunity to discuss the article
                    among ourselves and make sure we understand its implications. <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__2957" type="person">Mr. Richard Niebuhr</rs> has<pb
                        n="3"/> very kindly offered to assist us in this.</p>
                <p>Would it be possible for you to come to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__770"
                        type="place">New Haven</rs> some evening during <date from="1946-04-21"
                        to="1946-04-27">the week of April 21</date>? Unfortunately only Tuesday,
                    Wednesday, or Friday would be possible for the students in the group, most of
                    whom are very busy.</p>
                <p>If it would not be possible for you that week<pb n="4"/> perhaps you could come
                        <date from="1946-05-06" to="1946-05-12">the week of May 6<hi rend="sup"
                            >th</hi></date> (any night except Thursday) when we will be back from
                    spring recess.</p>
                <p>We would of course be glad to pay your expenses, and get you a room for the
                    night, should you care to stay in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__770" type="place"
                        >New Haven</rs>.</p>
                <p>I think it would be deeply appreciated by these students if you could manage to
                        come<pb n="5"/> for an evening. They are all impressed with the fact that
                        <rs ref="#tillich__MPIUNK3W" type="work">your article</rs> has the
                    intellectual content which they feel Christianity in general lacks.</p>
                <p>Hoping to hear from you in the near future.</p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely</salute><signed>
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3342" type="person">Edward Morris
                        </rs>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
